WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.600
Tim sat on his couch watching TV, while his girlfriend got ready and put her makeup on.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:05.740
It was her birthday.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:09.800
Well, technically, it was the day before, but that still counted as far as she was concerned.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:11.840
Tim offered to take her out to her favorite restaurant,

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.940
because the next night, on her actual birthday,

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:16.500
they are going to have a small party for her at their apartment.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:20.700
And so, this night, he thought it will be nice to celebrate just the two of them.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:23.240
They arrived at the restaurant and were seated by the hostess

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.580
after waiting for a few minutes in the reception area.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.580
They began looking at their menus and talking about this and that.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.520
Soon after, the waitress came and took their drink orders.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:35.500
After a few more minutes went by, Tim asked his girlfriend what she was thinking of ordering.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:36.760
Then, she asked him.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:40.800
They both said they weren't sure yet, and went down looking at their menus, continuing to talk.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.300
They talked about who is going to come to the party the next night, and what they still needed

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.200
to do beforehand to prepare for it.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:51.460
Then there was a little break in their conversation while they focused more seriously on making their final meal decisions.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:53.540
Tim decided what to order before her.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.680
Turkey tips.

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:58.040
He watched his girlfriend as she continued to inspect her menu.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.180
She was visibly stressed by the decision.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:04.560
Her brow was tight and her eyes jolted around as she flipped the menu pages back and forth.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:06.300
Tim thought about how funny this was.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:11.160
How she was furiously ruminating over which meal to choose, as if her life depended on it.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.240
"Such a simple, risk-free choice," he thought.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:16.400
Yet it seemed as if it carried the weight of the world on her in that moment.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.980
Tim looked around at all the other people in the restaurant.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:22.220
It looked as if about a quarter of them were looking at their menus as well.

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:26.000
He wondered how much of everyone's life was spent trying to make decisions like this.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:29.840
How much stress and worry were put on decisions as trivial as what meal to get

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:32.540
out of a few similarly good privileged meals.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:35.580
Then Tim realized that he sort of was just doing the same thing.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:40.580
This suddenly made Tim sort of anxious, as if this thought weirdly reminded him that he was a person:

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:45.920
A living thing in the world, and whatever absurdity he was looking at in the restaurant, he was also a part of.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:50.740
As he scanned around the room, he weirdly noticed the drowning chatter of all the other restaurant goers,

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:55.000
as if his ears pulled a hum of their voices from the background to the foreground of his attention.

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:58.000
He thought about how each individual voice made sense on their own,

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:00.240
but when heard collectively all at once,

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:04.840
they sort of sounded like squawking animal noises: completely indiscernible and bizarre.

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:06.760
This made Tim even more anxious.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.480
He tried to pull himself out of it.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.440
In his head, he told himself to relax, over and over.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:15.680
but in his attempt he found himself thinking about the conversation he was having with himself

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:17.940
He wondered who was telling who to relax.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:22.220
He thought about how he was somewhere inside his head, lodged within the object of his brain,

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:27.040
somehow looking out at all these other objects, thinking about them, trying to make sense of it all.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:29.100
He looked down at the chair he was sitting on.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:32.900
He thought about how many people were likely required for it to arrive there under him.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:36.000
He observed the wood frame, the leather skin of the cushion,

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:40.740
the pillowy material inside of it poking out of a hole, and all the little screws that held it together.

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:42.400
He wondered where it all came from.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:45.300
He thought about how he could trace each item back to something,

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:50.160
the wood from a tree, the leather from an animal or fabric, the metal from certain rocks in the ground,

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:53.360
the chair designed from other people; all of it from the planet.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:56.200
The planet from some swirling cluster of matter and energy.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:03:01.720
But then he suddenly became deeply overwhelmed by the idea that he didn't know where this string ended or began.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.200
...that no one really did.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:06.140
He started to feel somewhat claustrophobic and disoriented,

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:11.000
somehow disconnected from what was going on around him, yet deeply aware of everything at the same time.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:14.180
The chair almost looked unfamiliar to him as he continued looking at it.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:16.160
He thought about how it sort of just showed up,

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:18.280
how everything sort of just showed up.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:22.760
That one day, some amount of time ago, he realized he was Tim, and he showed up.

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:25.660
Another day, he learned what a chair was, and chairs showed up.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:28.920
Another day, he realized he was on this planet, and the planet showed up.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:32.800
And this continued on and on with everything he'd ever known and ever would.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.640
This then made Tim wonder what the chair would be if he wasn't there to sit in it,

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:38.620
if no one was anywhere to sit it in.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:41.120
He figured it probably wouldn't exist at all.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:45.240
But then he wondered what else wouldn't exist if there was no one to do anything with anything.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:49.000
If with no one to sit, there would be no chairs, then what would there be with no one to think?

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:51.080
No one to say what color anything is.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:54.540
What things sound like, what things feel like, what anything is like.

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:58.980
Tim suddenly became viscerally aware of the fact that he was looking out at everything through his eyeballs.

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:02.600
He thought that, surely, without any people, there would still remain objects.

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:05.140
Organizations of matter and energy floating around.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:08.760
But he considered the possibility that, with no one to say what purpose any of it had,

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:11.880
no one to say what made any one part of it different from any other,

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.300
then perhaps none of it would really be anything at all.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:18.360
He wondered in this moment if, in fact, everything he was looking at was actually nothing,

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:20.760
but somehow through him, it became everything.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:24.260
That here in this restaurant, he was creating existence as he lived through it,

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:29.360
determining what it all meant, and without him, without anyone, everything might as well be the same as nothi---

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:30.620
"So... are you ready to order?"

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:32.260
The waitress suddenly interrupted.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.920
Tim quickly realized he had slipped lower in his chair,

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:38.180
and felt a thin layer of sweat covering his forehead, back and arms.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:39.940
He wasn't sure how much time had passed,

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:43.040
but it looked as if his girlfriend was just looking back up from her menu.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:47.140
He felt like he was on the verge of passing out, struggling to properly catch his breath.

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:51.500
He looked fine from the outside, however; appearing no more than slightly distracted or tired.

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:54.720
His girlfriend said jokingly to him: "Hey, you there?"

00:04:55.000 --> 00:05:00.040
Tim paused for a short moment, then looked at her and said: "Yeah, I'm good," with a small laugh.

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:03.520
Then he and his girlfriend ordered, ate and went home.

